# Collected traces ARE committed (policy reversed 2026-08-30, IU).
#
# Upstream ignored llm/traces/ as "regenerated output". That premise does not
# hold here: these runs cost GPU-days on a shared cluster and cannot be
# regenerated cheaply, and at temperature 1.0 they cannot be regenerated
# identically at all. They are the irreplaceable research artifact
# (docs/STORAGE-POLICY.md §2), so they belong in version control.
#
# Cost is not the objection it looks like: git delta-compresses these
# near-identical JSON files at ~42x (measured on sl_lanes_L6, 74.8 MB -> 1.8
# MB), which beats per-file gzip's 23x while leaving the working copies as
# plain JSON that every reader script already handles.
#
# What is NOT committed: llama-server debug logs (382 MB, pure noise,
# regenerated on every run). Orchestrator telemetry IS committed -- the
# scaling-law report reads it.
llm/traces/logs/*.log
!llm/traces/logs/*_progress.jsonl

outputs/
results/
agora/output/

# Raw Polis open data — fetched from upstream (compdemocracy/openData), see
# polis-analysis/fetch_polis_data.sh. Not redistributed here.
datasets/polis-openData/

# NOTE: polis-analysis/output/*.json IS committed on purpose — reference
# artifacts for validating a fresh build_pipeline.py run.

# Secrets — never commit the real .env (ship .env.example only)
llm/.env
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
agora/.venv
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.numba_cache/

# OS
.DS_Store
